        "falsification_experiment.design"
      ],
      "description": "The dose is defined inconsistently. HfMo0.9V0.1TaTiZr and HfMo0.85V0.15TaTiZr replace 10% and 15% of the Mo sublattice, corresponding to only about 2 and 3 at.% V in the whole alloy. Elsewhere, 5, 10, and 15 at.% V are proposed as whole-alloy additions replacing Mo; 10–15 at.% whole-alloy V would replace 50–75% of the original equiatomic Mo and therefore violates the stated limit of less than 20% of Mo replaced."
    }
